load("@rules_venv//python/wasm:defs.bzl", "py_wasm_toolchain") py_wasm_toolchain(name, clang, compiler_files, cpython_libs, linkopts, pyconfig, python_version, stdlib, sysroot, wizer) Declare what py_wasm_module builds with: a C compiler for wasm32-wasi, a CPython built for it, and optionally Wizer. rules_venv registers toolchains of this kind for Python 3.13 and 3.14 on Linux and macOS hosts from archives it fetches (see extensions.bzl); a module that wants a compiler or a CPython of its own declares one and registers it with register_toolchains or --extra_toolchains. A toolchain is for one Python version: the headers that compile the module's host code and the interpreter that produces its bytecode are the rules_python toolchain's, so the two must be the same X.Y. Registering a toolchain with rules_python's is_python_X.Y as a target_setting, as below, makes it eligible only then, and a module's python_version selects it. Requirements: clang must be the clang of a wasi-sdk (this rule fails on any other driver), of the release that built cpython_libs, so that their wasi-libc match; cpython_libs holds libpython3.X.a and the static libraries of the modules compiled into it; pyconfig is that build's pyconfig.h, which stands in for the host one of the rules_python toolchain's headers; linkopts names what that build links against beyond libc, by default what CPython's own wasm32-wasi configuration uses. load("@rules_venv//python/wasm:defs.bzl", "py_wasm_toolchain") py_wasm_toolchain( name = "py_wasm_toolchain", clang = "@my_wasi_sdk//:bin/clang", compiler_files = "@my_wasi_sdk//:all_files", cpython_libs = "@my_cpython_wasi//:libs", pyconfig = "@my_cpython_wasi//:pyconfig.h", python_version = "3.14", stdlib = "@my_cpython_wasi_stdlib//:stdlib", wizer = "@my_wizer//:wizer",
) toolchain( name = "toolchain", exec_compatible_with = ["@platforms//os:linux", "@platforms//cpu:x86_64"], target_settings = ["@rules_python//python/config_settings:is_python_3.14"], toolchain = ":py_wasm_toolchain", toolchain_type = "@rules_venv//python/wasm:toolchain_type",
) ATTRIBUTES Name Description Type Mandatory Default name A unique name for this target. Name required clang The clang driver of a wasi-sdk, which also links. Label required compiler_files Every file of the wasi-sdk: the driver finds its resource directory and sysroot relative to itself. Label required cpython_libs libpython3.X.a and the static libraries of the modules compiled into it, from a CPython build for wasm32-wasi. Label required linkopts Linker flags for what cpython_libs needs beyond libc, after the libraries on the command line. The default is what CPython's wasm32-wasi configuration links: wasi-libc's emulated signals, getpid and process clocks, and dl and m. List of strings optional ["-ldl", "-lwasi-emulated-signal", "-lwasi-emulated-getpid", "-lwasi-emulated-process-clocks", "-lm"] pyconfig The pyconfig.h of that build, which describes wasm32-wasi to the headers. Label required python_version The X.Y of the CPython, e.g. 3.14. The rules_python toolchain a module builds with must be the same. String required stdlib The standard library of that CPython as source, with os.py at its root. Label required sysroot The sysroot, relative to the directory holding the driver's bin/. String optional "share/wasi-sysroot" wizer Wizer, to pre-initialize modules. Without it preinitialize cannot be used. Label optional None

